Emerging Market Opportunities
200 mm Silicon Carbide Manufacturing
The transition toward 200 mm SiC manufacturing creates opportunities to improve production scale and support higher-volume device supply. Infineon has introduced products using 200 mm SiC manufacturing technology, while other manufacturers are developing additional capacity and supply agreements. Commercial benefits will depend on production yields, substrate availability, and customer qualification.

GaN Adoption in Compact Power Systems
GaN devices can support compact, high-frequency power conversion in applications where switching speed and power density are important. Continued product development, volume production, and improved packaging provide opportunities in data center power supplies, consumer electronics, and industrial systems.

Grid Storage and Renewable Power Modules
Energy storage and renewable power systems require efficient conversion between electrical sources, batteries, and the grid. SiC-based modules can support selected high-power applications, creating opportunities for suppliers that provide reliable components and application engineering.

Data Center and Communications Infrastructure
Growing demand for computing and communications infrastructure creates opportunities for efficient power delivery and compact conversion systems. GaN and SiC devices can serve different power stages depending on voltage, switching frequency, thermal requirements, and system economics.

